WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:02:00.106 --> 00:02:01.482
I must see the queen.

3
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.364
Your Grace.

4
00:02:21.544 --> 00:02:23.962
He is risen.

5
00:02:23.963 --> 00:02:26.423
- Who?
- Aegon!

6
00:02:26.424 --> 00:02:27.884
Sunfyre is alive.

7
00:02:29.051 --> 00:02:30.052
Out!

8
00:02:32.889 --> 00:02:35.432
Sunfyre is dead.
rotting in a wasteland.

9
00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.312
- Oh.
- Sit down.

10
00:02:39.979 --> 00:02:42.773
Aegon burned
the Mooton host

11
00:02:42.774 --> 00:02:45.485
at Rook's Rest.
and then flew...

12
00:02:46.819 --> 00:02:48.446
I don't know where.

13
00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.409
His supporters have already sent
ravens throughout the realm...

14
00:02:54.577 --> 00:02:57.412
announcing the king's return.

15
00:02:57.413 --> 00:02:59.122
The smallfolk name it
a sign from the gods

16
00:02:59.123 --> 00:03:01.249
that Aegon is ordained to rule.
that he and his dragon

17
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:03.920
have been resurrected
to reclaim the throne.

18
00:03:04.462 --> 00:03:07.088
At this moment.
mine own subjects

19
00:03:07.089 --> 00:03:09.257
gather outside the Grand Sept.
beseeching the gods

20
00:03:09.258 --> 00:03:10.842
to say who is meant
to rule them.

21
00:03:10.843 --> 00:03:13.512
After all for which
I have fought and suffered!

22
00:03:13.513 --> 00:03:14.514
Rhaenyra.

23
00:03:26.526 --> 00:03:29.152
The lesser gods have no say
in what is to come.

24
00:03:29.153 --> 00:03:30.988
We are the blood
of Old Valyria.

25
00:03:33.199 --> 00:03:35.660
You have an absolute power
within your grasp.

26
00:03:36.786 --> 00:03:38.287
You have only to wield it.

27
00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:42.291
Fucking Viserys!

28
00:03:44.627 --> 00:03:47.128
He put me here.

29
00:03:47.129 --> 00:03:49.214
His prophecy has tested me
again and again.

30
00:03:49.215 --> 00:03:51.550
and I have met
its every challenge!

31
00:05:54.423 --> 00:05:55.924
Your Grace.
have plans been laid

32
00:05:55.925 --> 00:05:57.259
for the Sea Snake's rescue?

33
00:05:59.428 --> 00:06:00.972
There will be a rescue?

34
00:06:03.432 --> 00:06:05.100
Your father
will search Tumbleton

35
00:06:05.101 --> 00:06:06.768
for the Sea Snake once the town
has been reclaimed.

36
00:06:06.769 --> 00:06:09.104
He'll be long dead by then.

37
00:06:09.105 --> 00:06:11.272
Send me now.

38
00:06:11.273 --> 00:06:13.608
You and Addam are needed here
to guard the city.

39
00:06:13.609 --> 00:06:16.152
if indeed these rumors are true

40
00:06:16.153 --> 00:06:17.947
and Sunfyre
was allowed to live.

41
00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:21.783
Corlys is your Hand.
your oldest ally.

42
00:06:21.784 --> 00:06:23.368
I do not wish
your grandsire ill.

43
00:06:23.369 --> 00:06:25.120
but he made his choice.

44
00:06:25.121 --> 00:06:26.872
and we must now
pay its price.

45
00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.626
It was your fault.

46
00:06:32.753 --> 00:06:34.004
What?

47
00:06:34.005 --> 00:06:36.214
That Lord Corlys
was out there to be taken.

48
00:06:36.215 --> 00:06:37.967
You do not dare.

49
00:06:38.843 --> 00:06:41.053
It is how you've always
treated those who serve you.

50
00:06:42.513 --> 00:06:45.056
Addam and I have labored
without rest

51
00:06:45.057 --> 00:06:47.559
over countless sorties
in search of your enemies.

52
00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.477
only to be repaid
in your anger.

53
00:06:49.478 --> 00:06:51.396
Yes. that is because
your sorties

54
00:06:51.397 --> 00:06:54.649
have yielded nothing.
while my enemies

55
00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.484
have been allowed
to muster their strength.

56
00:06:56.485 --> 00:06:59.155
If a person is useful to you.
you wield them.

57
00:07:00.364 --> 00:07:01.824
But if not.
you abandon them

58
00:07:02.742 --> 00:07:04.159
as you have with Rhaena.

59
00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:07.162
And now. she is broken.
like my grandsire.

60
00:07:07.163 --> 00:07:09.999
I would have been justified in
abandoning you after the Gullet.

61
00:07:11.333 --> 00:07:12.334
Perhaps.

62
00:07:13.335 --> 00:07:14.587
But you need my dragon.

63
00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:19.759
Insolent child.

64
00:07:21.552 --> 00:07:23.386
I should not blame you
for it truly.

65
00:07:23.387 --> 00:07:24.847
Insolence runs in your blood.

66
00:07:26.098 --> 00:07:28.184
As your sister
has lately reminded us.

67
00:07:40.696 --> 00:07:42.739
Good morrow. my lords.

68
00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.033
"Good morrow." indeed.

69
00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:47.452
We've just sailed through
the night from Driftmark.

70
00:07:47.453 --> 00:07:50.706
after learning our Lord Admiral
is hostage to the Hightowers.

71
00:07:51.749 --> 00:07:55.211
The queen has called upon you
to secure King's Landing.

72
00:07:57.213 --> 00:07:59.589
To answer her could mean
our lord's death.

73
00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:02.384
Lord Corlys knew of the risks
of his adventures.

74
00:08:03.886 --> 00:08:06.471
He would want us to appraise
Velaryon honor

75
00:08:06.472 --> 00:08:07.890
as greater than his life.

76
00:08:09.141 --> 00:08:11.727
Who are you to speak
to our lord's desires?

77
00:08:13.229 --> 00:08:14.897
His eldest living son.

78
00:08:17.566 --> 00:08:18.984
And named successor.

79
00:08:20.945 --> 00:08:24.448
Your once and future
Lord of the Tides.

80
00:08:29.745 --> 00:08:31.455
Open the gates!

81
00:08:46.512 --> 00:08:47.638
About face!

82
00:08:48.848 --> 00:08:50.266
Forward march!

83
00:09:00.359 --> 00:09:01.360
That...

84
00:09:02.611 --> 00:09:05.322
all of it. is for you.

85
00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:09.618
Remarkable. is it not?

86
00:09:13.455 --> 00:09:14.456
But...

87
00:09:15.708 --> 00:09:17.501
you must be made a knight...

88
00:09:18.794 --> 00:09:20.462
before you can be crowned king.

89
00:09:21.839 --> 00:09:22.840
Kneel.

90
00:09:35.019 --> 00:09:36.895
Daeron Targaryen.

91
00:09:36.896 --> 00:09:40.190
do you swear before the eyes
of gods and men

92
00:09:40.191 --> 00:09:43.484
to defend those
who cannot defend themselves...

93
00:09:43.485 --> 00:09:46.529
Everyone inside!

94
00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:49.532
<i>...to protect all women
and children...</i>

95
00:09:49.533 --> 00:09:51.577
Come back here! Back!

96
00:09:52.494 --> 00:09:55.580
<i>...to obey your captains.
your liege lord...</i>

97
00:09:55.581 --> 00:09:57.207
Seal the gates!

98
00:09:57.208 --> 00:09:59.335
<i>...to fight bravely whenever needed...</i>

99
00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:02.921
<i>and to do such other tasks</i>

100
00:10:02.922 --> 00:10:04.672
<i>- as are laid upon you...</i>
- Steady!

101
00:10:04.673 --> 00:10:06.174
<i>- ...however hard...</i>
- Hoist!

102
00:10:06.175 --> 00:10:08.885
<i>...or humble
or dangerous they may be?</i>

103
00:10:08.886 --> 00:10:09.887
Halt!

104
00:10:14.266 --> 00:10:15.434
I swear it.

105
00:10:22.942 --> 00:10:24.693
Then. rise a knight.

106
00:10:30.532 --> 00:10:32.368
Ser Daeron the Daring.

107
00:10:35.287 --> 00:10:37.206
And light the way.

108
00:10:49.093 --> 00:10:52.429
The Queen of Bastards' armies
are at the gates.

109
00:10:53.764 --> 00:10:56.099
And leading them
to the slaughter

110
00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:58.559
will be her uncle.
No.

111
00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:00.478
Her lover.

112
00:11:00.479 --> 00:11:02.731
No.
Her husband.

113
00:11:04.566 --> 00:11:07.361
Daemon fucking Targaryen.

114
00:11:08.445 --> 00:11:11.240
- And his dragon.
- Of course he's got a fucking dragon!

115
00:11:13.909 --> 00:11:15.327
But he's not gonna use it.

116
00:11:17.579 --> 00:11:19.163
And how do you know?

117
00:11:19.164 --> 00:11:23.252
'Cause his lady wife.
the queen. won't let him.

118
00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:27.631
Rhaenyra's got Daemon
on a short lead.

119
00:11:28.757 --> 00:11:31.260
Like a bitch in a kennel.

120
00:11:34.263 --> 00:11:36.265
Another ale for the dragonlord.

121
00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:42.270
The Rogue Prince
will soon quake

122
00:11:42.271 --> 00:11:46.691
before the mighty and terrible

123
00:11:46.692 --> 00:11:48.777
Lord Ulf the White!

124
00:11:56.368 --> 00:11:57.786
Your Grace.

125
00:11:59.621 --> 00:12:01.372
Y-Your Grace.
is aught amiss?

126
00:12:01.373 --> 00:12:02.624
What is it?

127
00:12:03.959 --> 00:12:05.836
The Princess Helaena.

128
00:12:06.795 --> 00:12:08.547
She still has not taken food.

129
00:12:09.798 --> 00:12:12.342
The maesters
worry for her health.

130
00:12:12.343 --> 00:12:14.636
especially for the babe
in her belly.

131
00:12:20.559 --> 00:12:21.977
Summon Ser Alyn.

132
00:12:25.022 --> 00:12:27.149
I require a full escort
to the Grand Sept.

133
00:12:27.816 --> 00:12:31.486
There. today.
the High Septon will anoint me

134
00:12:31.487 --> 00:12:34.073
and bless my reign for all
of King's Landing to see.

135
00:12:35.157 --> 00:12:37.659
There will be no doubt who
the gods have chosen to rule.

136
00:12:39.161 --> 00:12:40.662
At once. Your Grace.

137
00:12:42.206 --> 00:12:43.499
Will that be all?

138
00:12:50.172 --> 00:12:51.173
No.

139
00:12:58.847 --> 00:12:59.932
What is this?

140
00:13:00.724 --> 00:13:01.933
Sers.

141
00:13:01.934 --> 00:13:04.143
- Sers!
- My lady.

142
00:13:04.144 --> 00:13:06.771
Beg pardon for the intrusion.
We weren't given much time.

143
00:13:06.772 --> 00:13:08.356
Time for what?

144
00:13:08.357 --> 00:13:11.025
Your passage has been arranged aboard
the <i>Mermaid's Kiss.</i>

145
00:13:11.026 --> 00:13:13.861
You are to sail
for Pentos at dusk.

146
00:13:13.862 --> 00:13:16.572
I am to inform you

147
00:13:16.573 --> 00:13:18.533
that your services here
are at an end.

148
00:13:20.077 --> 00:13:22.954
You have served the queen
and the realm most faithfully.

149
00:13:22.955 --> 00:13:25.540
and Her Grace wishes
to extend her gratitude.

150
00:13:27.292 --> 00:13:29.794
You will be provided with gold
sufficient for a manse

151
00:13:29.795 --> 00:13:31.380
and servants of your own.

152
00:13:34.550 --> 00:13:35.884
Be quick about it.

153
00:13:39.388 --> 00:13:41.932
I... I do not understand either.
my lady.

154
00:13:53.485 --> 00:13:55.446
The hour has passed.
my lady.

155
00:13:57.573 --> 00:13:59.408
I must return you
to your quarters.

156
00:14:22.598 --> 00:14:24.266
This way. princess.

157
00:14:40.699 --> 00:14:42.617
Do not trust the queen.

158
00:14:42.618 --> 00:14:44.952
Aegon has returned.
His dragon lives.

159
00:14:44.953 --> 00:14:47.288
Your unborn child
is a hostage.

160
00:14:47.289 --> 00:14:49.790
a prize by which
she can hold power

161
00:14:49.791 --> 00:14:51.334
- over her enemies.
- Keep moving.

162
00:14:51.335 --> 00:14:53.545
- Enough.
- She will never release you.

163
00:15:04.556 --> 00:15:06.307
<i>Do you remember?</i>

164
00:15:06.308 --> 00:15:09.353
<i>Do you remember?</i>

165
00:15:12.189 --> 00:15:13.482
<i>Help me.</i>

166
00:15:16.652 --> 00:15:18.361
Fret not.

167
00:15:18.362 --> 00:15:19.655
You're alive.

168
00:15:22.157 --> 00:15:23.241
Here.

169
00:15:23.242 --> 00:15:24.493
Drink this.

170
00:15:26.245 --> 00:15:27.663
There'll be another in an hour.

171
00:15:29.081 --> 00:15:31.165
She poisoned me.

172
00:15:31.166 --> 00:15:34.585
You have realized
you're alone in this world.

173
00:15:34.586 --> 00:15:36.171
In that. we are together.

174
00:15:45.097 --> 00:15:47.182
But I no longer wish
to suffer it.

175
00:15:49.685 --> 00:15:51.185
Do you?

176
00:15:51.186 --> 00:15:53.021
Why do you care
whether I am alone?

177
00:15:54.523 --> 00:15:56.525
Whether I live or die?

178
00:15:59.695 --> 00:16:02.114
I'm a kinslayer. Alys.

179
00:16:04.032 --> 00:16:07.661
My own brother
is dead by my hand.

180
00:16:08.412 --> 00:16:11.707
I have been damned for my trespasses
and cursed to suffer.

181
00:16:14.293 --> 00:16:16.461
You should abandon me.

182
00:16:18.005 --> 00:16:20.299
Lest you bring mine own fate
upon yourself.

183
00:16:26.847 --> 00:16:29.640
When the dragon Balerion
burned this place.

184
00:16:29.641 --> 00:16:31.935
it was to end
Lord Harren's line.

185
00:16:33.437 --> 00:16:35.897
But his line
was not so easily ended.

186
00:16:37.399 --> 00:16:38.567
A child. a...

187
00:16:39.943 --> 00:16:40.944
a boy...

188
00:16:42.738 --> 00:16:43.905
lived on.

189
00:16:44.906 --> 00:16:47.826
Burned terribly.
but alive.

190
00:16:49.911 --> 00:16:52.414
His mother would have
given anything to save him.

191
00:16:56.251 --> 00:17:00.171
She summoned maesters
from across the Seven Kingdoms.

192
00:17:00.172 --> 00:17:01.506
but to no avail.

193
00:17:08.597 --> 00:17:10.932
So. she turned to older cures.

194
00:17:12.184 --> 00:17:15.853
She uncovered incantations
more ancient than the land.

195
00:17:15.854 --> 00:17:19.441
She treated with things
that lived in the forest.

196
00:17:22.653 --> 00:17:25.947
But none of it could unmake
what dragonfire made.

197
00:17:27.866 --> 00:17:29.326
And when the boy was gone...

198
00:17:36.458 --> 00:17:38.794
she tr... she tried
to go with him.

199
00:17:49.638 --> 00:17:52.140
And that is when
she learned the cost.

200
00:17:58.397 --> 00:18:00.649
She discovered then
she was cursed.

201
00:18:01.316 --> 00:18:02.567
To live on...

202
00:18:04.361 --> 00:18:08.573
to remain within the bounds
of the river kings of old...

203
00:18:09.491 --> 00:18:12.034
cursed for sharing
in Harren's avarice.

204
00:18:12.035 --> 00:18:14.995
Stripped of her name.
her title.

205
00:18:14.996 --> 00:18:16.415
her castle.

206
00:18:18.333 --> 00:18:21.210
And sentenced to serve
every ha'penny lord

207
00:18:21.211 --> 00:18:23.003
who came here to rule it.

208
00:18:23.004 --> 00:18:25.548
That was a hundred years past.

209
00:18:25.549 --> 00:18:27.592
It's a long time
to be alone.

210
00:18:56.371 --> 00:18:58.081
You must eat. sister.

211
00:19:04.713 --> 00:19:06.089
Think of the babe.

212
00:19:07.048 --> 00:19:08.759
You are thinking
of him now. too?

213
00:19:10.469 --> 00:19:13.722
You're saying it's a boy?
Do you know this?

214
00:19:16.141 --> 00:19:17.309
Look at me.

215
00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:28.904
You cannot think
I would harm you.

216
00:19:29.696 --> 00:19:32.616
Do you think life is nothing
more than not being dead?

217
00:19:36.828 --> 00:19:39.247
Our father
would hate you for this.

218
00:19:42.334 --> 00:19:44.503
And yet he did nothing
to prevent it.

219
00:19:45.796 --> 00:19:49.256
I strove to honor
his philosophy

220
00:19:49.257 --> 00:19:51.926
until I saw that it would be
the realm's undoing.

221
00:19:51.927 --> 00:19:56.430
There is a beetle that emerges
on the cusp of summer.

222
00:19:56.431 --> 00:19:58.140
It has lots of colors.

223
00:19:58.141 --> 00:20:01.436
Blue. gold. purples.

224
00:20:02.771 --> 00:20:04.314
It looks like a turtle.

225
00:20:06.107 --> 00:20:07.818
Have you ever noticed it?

226
00:20:09.027 --> 00:20:10.653
I can't say I have.

227
00:20:10.654 --> 00:20:13.447
You can only find it
in King's Landing.

228
00:20:13.448 --> 00:20:16.827
It sustains itself on the waste
of other creatures.

229
00:20:21.498 --> 00:20:22.624
It's beautiful.

230
00:20:25.627 --> 00:20:27.963
Well. when summer returns.
you will have to show me.

231
00:20:35.053 --> 00:20:36.972
You don't care about it.

232
00:20:39.641 --> 00:20:40.809
You're pretending.

233
00:20:42.894 --> 00:20:47.148
All the things you care about
are ugly.

234
00:20:48.984 --> 00:20:50.569
This place...

235
00:20:51.820 --> 00:20:53.029
is ugly.

236
00:20:56.825 --> 00:20:58.994
You. yourself...

237
00:21:00.495 --> 00:21:01.662
ugly.

238
00:21:01.663 --> 00:21:02.664
Eat.

239
00:21:03.957 --> 00:21:05.667
Or you will force my hand.

240
00:21:34.029 --> 00:21:35.030
No.

241
00:21:35.947 --> 00:21:37.198
No! No!

242
00:21:37.949 --> 00:21:40.200
No! No! No!

243
00:21:40.201 --> 00:21:42.036
Stop! Stop.

244
00:21:57.469 --> 00:21:59.054
Forward march!

245
00:22:10.774 --> 00:22:11.775
Brother.

246
00:22:13.443 --> 00:22:15.319
Will you march
on Tumbleton as well?

247
00:22:15.320 --> 00:22:17.739
No. Today we guard the queen
in her purpose.

248
00:22:19.074 --> 00:22:20.450
Where does she go?

249
00:22:24.913 --> 00:22:28.540
News of Aegon's return has set
the queen on a dark path.

250
00:22:28.541 --> 00:22:31.251
She has grounded Baela
and confined her to the Keep.

251
00:22:31.252 --> 00:22:32.920
Did you know this?

252
00:22:32.921 --> 00:22:34.922
These are dangerous days.

253
00:22:34.923 --> 00:22:37.759
and it is not mine
to question Her Grace.

254
00:22:40.595 --> 00:22:42.096
Why would you?

255
00:22:42.097 --> 00:22:45.432
While our father awaits
the Hightower gallows.

256
00:22:45.433 --> 00:22:48.268
Rhaenyra raises you up
in his place.

257
00:22:48.269 --> 00:22:50.604
A glorious ascent for a bastard.

258
00:22:53.441 --> 00:22:56.945
I have no ambition
but to discharge my duty.

259
00:22:58.154 --> 00:23:00.030
Be ready!

260
00:23:14.295 --> 00:23:15.462
Form up!

261
00:23:15.463 --> 00:23:16.631
Form up!

262
00:23:22.554 --> 00:23:23.555
March!

263
00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:45.326
Gods.

264
00:23:46.911 --> 00:23:48.496
How will we face them all?

265
00:23:49.664 --> 00:23:52.542
Bravely and pointlessly.

266
00:23:53.668 --> 00:23:55.836
Take your places. boys.

267
00:23:55.837 --> 00:23:57.922
Keep coming. take your places.

268
00:23:59.591 --> 00:24:01.051
Keep coming. Be brave.

269
00:24:02.802 --> 00:24:05.055
Put the boys to the front.
They must be seen.

270
00:24:07.015 --> 00:24:10.100
My lord. Ulf hasn't reported.

271
00:24:10.101 --> 00:24:11.519
and he's not with his dragon.

272
00:24:16.941 --> 00:24:18.859
Take a tithing of men
off each post.

273
00:24:18.860 --> 00:24:19.860
Search the town.

274
00:24:19.861 --> 00:24:20.944
Find him.

275
00:24:20.945 --> 00:24:22.112
You! With me.

276
00:24:22.113 --> 00:24:23.698
- Something's wrong.
- Yes.

277
00:24:24.616 --> 00:24:26.408
We're all going to die.

278
00:24:26.409 --> 00:24:27.577
No.

279
00:24:28.244 --> 00:24:29.704
With Uncle.

280
00:24:30.705 --> 00:24:33.249
He and Roxton
have some secret plot afoot.

281
00:24:35.585 --> 00:24:37.252
He has kept it even from me.

282
00:24:37.253 --> 00:24:39.463
- Whatever it was...
- Get away from me!

283
00:24:39.464 --> 00:24:41.966
...it has not appeared
to have come to pass.

284
00:24:45.220 --> 00:24:46.595
Please!

285
00:24:46.596 --> 00:24:48.138
Please. ser.
we don't want to do it.

286
00:24:48.139 --> 00:24:49.723
- I just want to go home to my mom.
- Don't make us.

287
00:24:50.934 --> 00:24:52.644
I must take wing
against the enemy.

288
00:24:53.812 --> 00:24:54.813
No!

289
00:24:55.980 --> 00:24:59.901
All these men. these boys.
are here for me.

290
00:25:01.569 --> 00:25:04.363
- I cannot let them fight alone.
- For what purpose. boy?

291
00:25:04.364 --> 00:25:06.573
To become another body
amongst Ormund's countless dead?

292
00:25:06.574 --> 00:25:08.659
What are my choices?

293
00:25:08.660 --> 00:25:11.329
I either fight. or I flee.

294
00:25:17.460 --> 00:25:19.087
Mayhaps there is another.

295
00:25:21.923 --> 00:25:23.341
Dragon!

296
00:25:40.358 --> 00:25:42.110
Ulf the Dragonrider!

297
00:25:43.278 --> 00:25:45.362
I'm looking for
Ulf the Dragonrider.

298
00:25:45.363 --> 00:25:47.699
Ulf!

299
00:25:48.658 --> 00:25:49.951
Ulf!

300
00:25:54.372 --> 00:25:58.208
And now. Lord Ormund's boy king
and his faithful squire.

301
00:25:58.209 --> 00:25:59.793
Shut up.

302
00:25:59.794 --> 00:26:02.838
Driftmark lies in ruin.
your legacy in tatters.

303
00:26:02.839 --> 00:26:06.550
But King Daeron. in all
his generosity and wisdom.

304
00:26:06.551 --> 00:26:07.885
can offer a richer future

305
00:26:07.886 --> 00:26:10.179
than the one Rhaenyra
has laid for you.

306
00:26:10.180 --> 00:26:12.223
My honor is all
that remains to me.

307
00:26:13.641 --> 00:26:16.894
Do you really think I would
hawk it for Hightower coin?

308
00:26:16.895 --> 00:26:18.687
Very well.

309
00:26:18.688 --> 00:26:20.231
The hard road. then.

310
00:26:37.582 --> 00:26:38.708
Make way!

311
00:26:39.834 --> 00:26:41.085
Clear the way!

312
00:26:42.378 --> 00:26:45.757
- Move back!
- Get back! Get back!

313
00:26:46.507 --> 00:26:48.760
Move! Clear the way!

314
00:26:50.011 --> 00:26:52.013
Get back!

315
00:27:07.362 --> 00:27:08.863
Get back!

316
00:27:15.036 --> 00:27:16.954
You are my heir now. Joffrey.

317
00:27:16.955 --> 00:27:19.331
and the duty I pass to you

318
00:27:19.332 --> 00:27:21.042
is more than simple rule.

319
00:27:24.212 --> 00:27:27.214
There is a story
that your grandsire told me.

320
00:27:27.215 --> 00:27:29.384
It was told to him
by the Old King.

321
00:27:30.468 --> 00:27:32.303
And I passed it on...

322
00:27:33.596 --> 00:27:34.889
to your brother...

323
00:27:36.766 --> 00:27:38.642
following mine own ascent.

324
00:27:44.399 --> 00:27:46.566
Tumbleton. my lords!

325
00:27:46.567 --> 00:27:47.819
At long last.

326
00:27:49.904 --> 00:27:51.405
If it weren't for Cole.

327
00:27:51.406 --> 00:27:52.823
we'd have been here
a fortnight ago.

328
00:27:52.824 --> 00:27:55.784
So easy to forget about him.
Do tell me how he died.

329
00:27:55.785 --> 00:27:56.952
Badly.

330
00:28:00.248 --> 00:28:03.417
My prince. my lords.
a Hightower knight approaches.

331
00:28:03.418 --> 00:28:05.669
So? Kill him.

332
00:28:05.670 --> 00:28:07.005
With Lord Corlys.

333
00:28:09.299 --> 00:28:10.424
Hyah.

334
00:28:23.104 --> 00:28:25.147
Prince Daemon.

335
00:28:25.148 --> 00:28:26.773
I am Ser Gwayne Hightower.

336
00:28:26.774 --> 00:28:28.483
Well met.

337
00:28:28.484 --> 00:28:29.986
Fuck me.

338
00:28:32.739 --> 00:28:34.949
I've seen more meat
on a butcher's knife.

339
00:28:36.951 --> 00:28:38.285
Can I kill him?

340
00:28:38.286 --> 00:28:40.704
You already know Lord Corlys.

341
00:28:40.705 --> 00:28:41.789
Are you well?

342
00:28:42.832 --> 00:28:43.875
I'm well enough.

343
00:28:46.711 --> 00:28:48.378
So. speak.

344
00:28:48.379 --> 00:28:51.465
My cousin Ormund
has taken leave of his senses.

345
00:28:51.466 --> 00:28:53.175
He would rather die
than admit defeat.

346
00:28:53.176 --> 00:28:54.302
And you?

347
00:28:55.178 --> 00:28:56.637
Well. I'm not blind.

348
00:28:57.847 --> 00:28:59.974
I know we will not survive
the day if you attack.

349
00:29:01.225 --> 00:29:02.810
So. as a token of good faith...

350
00:29:06.481 --> 00:29:08.482
I return your Hand.

351
00:29:08.483 --> 00:29:11.486
Four fingers of him. at least.

352
00:29:12.236 --> 00:29:13.487
I have come to sue for peace.

353
00:29:13.488 --> 00:29:15.655
To plead with you

354
00:29:15.656 --> 00:29:17.491
at the behest
of Daeron Targaryen.

355
00:29:17.492 --> 00:29:21.411
The latest
in your line of false kings.

356
00:29:21.412 --> 00:29:22.996
The war will end
when all the traitors' heads

357
00:29:22.997 --> 00:29:25.083
are mounted on spikes
above the King's Gate...

358
00:29:26.084 --> 00:29:27.250
and not before.

359
00:29:27.251 --> 00:29:29.045
Listen to Daeron's entreaty.

360
00:29:29.837 --> 00:29:31.213
Divide the realm.

361
00:29:31.214 --> 00:29:33.340
Let the queen rule
over the Crownlands. the North.

362
00:29:33.341 --> 00:29:35.175
the Vale. all the lands
watered by the Trident.

363
00:29:35.176 --> 00:29:38.220
and let Daeron
rule from Oldtown.

364
00:29:38.221 --> 00:29:39.931
Oh. please!

365
00:29:41.099 --> 00:29:44.351
Let me kill this milk-suck
southerling cunt.

366
00:29:44.352 --> 00:29:46.395
The realm was once
seven kingdoms.

367
00:29:46.396 --> 00:29:48.063
before the Conqueror.
when we were divided

368
00:29:48.064 --> 00:29:49.523
- but at peace...
- Stop!

369
00:29:49.524 --> 00:29:51.400
My good Lord Hand.

370
00:29:51.401 --> 00:29:53.151
I thought the Hightowers

371
00:29:53.152 --> 00:29:55.071
might have cut off
your tongue as well.

372
00:29:58.116 --> 00:29:59.450
Hightower is not wrong.

373
00:30:00.410 --> 00:30:02.411
There are great houses
who still hold to the precedent

374
00:30:02.412 --> 00:30:06.206
set by the Great Council
that a woman cannot rule.

375
00:30:06.207 --> 00:30:08.750
It was your wife
who was passed over. Corlys.

376
00:30:08.751 --> 00:30:10.877
Rhaenyra seized the throne
with a horde of dragons.

377
00:30:10.878 --> 00:30:12.379
Her rule is now unassailable.

378
00:30:12.380 --> 00:30:14.464
The queen
has many dragons. yes.

379
00:30:14.465 --> 00:30:16.050
but the great houses hesitate.

380
00:30:17.218 --> 00:30:19.929
Her subjects do not feel safe.
nor should they.

381
00:30:21.055 --> 00:30:22.932
Aemond and Vhagar
remain at large.

382
00:30:29.897 --> 00:30:31.815
Give Prince Daeron Oldtown.

383
00:30:31.816 --> 00:30:35.068
Name him Lord Paramount
of the Reach.

384
00:30:35.069 --> 00:30:37.320
Daeron will never be king.

385
00:30:37.321 --> 00:30:39.781
but he and his dragon
can be wardens of the South.

386
00:30:39.782 --> 00:30:41.826
That wasn't what I was offering.

387
00:30:44.495 --> 00:30:46.288
Wed Daeron to Rhaena.

388
00:30:46.289 --> 00:30:48.248
Seal the breach
between your houses.

389
00:30:48.249 --> 00:30:50.500
With the combined will
of King's Landing.

390
00:30:50.501 --> 00:30:52.794
the Reach. the North.
the Riverlands.

391
00:30:52.795 --> 00:30:55.088
and the Vale. Rhaenyra
can quickly bring the West

392
00:30:55.089 --> 00:30:57.340
and the Stormlands to heel.

393
00:30:57.341 --> 00:30:59.092
And what will
the usurper Aegon say

394
00:30:59.093 --> 00:31:01.011
when he hears of this pact?

395
00:31:01.012 --> 00:31:04.598
He now scuttles about somewhere
on his crippled dragon.

396
00:31:04.599 --> 00:31:07.100
half-cooked.
but still fit to rule.

397
00:31:07.101 --> 00:31:08.686
Or so he thinks.

398
00:31:10.104 --> 00:31:11.355
Was that news?

399
00:31:12.940 --> 00:31:15.901
It is so tragic to see
brother set against brother.

400
00:31:15.902 --> 00:31:18.612
Aegon and Aemond would be
common enemies of this new alliance.

401
00:31:18.613 --> 00:31:19.989
Alliance?

402
00:31:21.240 --> 00:31:25.160
I never took you for a traitor.
Corlys. and worse. a craven.

403
00:31:25.161 --> 00:31:27.872
What price has the boy king
offered for your fealty?

404
00:31:29.040 --> 00:31:30.041
Peace.

405
00:31:31.292 --> 00:31:34.294
Two paths
diverge before you. Daemon.

406
00:31:34.295 --> 00:31:36.296
but both lead to the same end.

407
00:31:36.297 --> 00:31:40.467
Rhaenyra sitting the Iron Throne
ruling the Seven Kingdoms.

408
00:31:40.468 --> 00:31:42.178
All that remains
for you to decide...

409
00:31:43.638 --> 00:31:46.348
is what you want
from this war.

410
00:31:46.349 --> 00:31:47.642
Victory?

411
00:31:49.143 --> 00:31:50.853
Or a mountain
of dead Hightowers?

412
00:31:52.313 --> 00:31:54.231
What do you think?

413
00:31:54.232 --> 00:31:56.566
You would callously cast away
the lives of thou...

414
00:31:59.195 --> 00:32:01.655
No one will rule but Rhaenyra.

415
00:32:01.656 --> 00:32:04.241
the ordained Queen of the Andals.
of the First Men.

416
00:32:04.242 --> 00:32:06.493
of beggars and thieves
and cowards like you.

417
00:32:06.494 --> 00:32:08.828
A new Valyria
will rise from the ashes

418
00:32:08.829 --> 00:32:10.539
of her usurper half-brothers

419
00:32:10.540 --> 00:32:12.707
and of the Hightowers
of Oldtown.

420
00:32:12.708 --> 00:32:16.044
Now. you came to me
under a banner of peace.

421
00:32:16.045 --> 00:32:18.171
so I will give you the choice.

422
00:32:18.172 --> 00:32:21.383
Die here.
or behind those walls.

423
00:32:21.384 --> 00:32:23.719
like the rodent you are.

424
00:32:26.180 --> 00:32:27.722
Lord Corlys is my prisoner.

425
00:32:27.723 --> 00:32:29.599
Hightower may return
to alert his cousin

426
00:32:29.600 --> 00:32:32.769
- to our imminent coming.
- Get up! Get up!

427
00:32:32.770 --> 00:32:34.229
Bring the ladders and the rams

428
00:32:34.230 --> 00:32:35.689
and form up to march.

429
00:32:35.690 --> 00:32:37.899
The next man
to stall on this attack

430
00:32:37.900 --> 00:32:41.695
will be tied to the front
of my fucking horse!

431
00:33:46.469 --> 00:33:47.928
It cannot be.

432
00:33:48.971 --> 00:33:50.306
You are dead.

433
00:33:56.437 --> 00:33:57.688
I'm alive!

434
00:33:59.607 --> 00:34:00.608
Imbecile.

435
00:34:03.611 --> 00:34:06.112
Brother. Brother.

436
00:34:06.113 --> 00:34:07.990
I beg for your forgiveness.

437
00:34:19.627 --> 00:34:20.836
Forgiveness?

438
00:34:24.965 --> 00:34:26.967
I should split you in half.

439
00:34:29.804 --> 00:34:30.805
Hm?

440
00:34:32.473 --> 00:34:34.809
I should have Sunfyre
burn you alive.

441
00:34:36.060 --> 00:34:39.397
Mm. but slowly.

442
00:34:40.815 --> 00:34:42.817
So I can see your skin...

443
00:34:43.859 --> 00:34:46.821
peel and blister.

444
00:34:47.530 --> 00:34:48.989
You kinslayer.

445
00:34:50.991 --> 00:34:52.743
You usurper.

446
00:34:54.870 --> 00:34:55.871
You cunt!

447
00:35:04.338 --> 00:35:05.339
No.

448
00:35:07.550 --> 00:35:10.510
No. no. no. no. no. no. no!

449
00:35:10.511 --> 00:35:12.178
I was supposed to enjoy this.

450
00:35:12.179 --> 00:35:13.556
What's wrong with you?

451
00:35:15.850 --> 00:35:17.017
Fight me!

452
00:35:21.897 --> 00:35:24.357
I coveted what you had

453
00:35:24.358 --> 00:35:26.109
and judged you unsuited
for the crown.

454
00:35:26.110 --> 00:35:27.527
Oh.

455
00:35:31.699 --> 00:35:33.367
I tried to kill you
to take your place.

456
00:35:35.703 --> 00:35:38.038
You'd be right
to sentence me to die.

457
00:35:44.128 --> 00:35:45.212
Fuck you.

458
00:35:47.089 --> 00:35:48.090
Get up.

459
00:35:55.890 --> 00:35:57.307
We're going to Tumbleton.

460
00:35:57.308 --> 00:36:00.060
My prince cannot.
His dragon abandoned him.

461
00:36:01.228 --> 00:36:03.773
- Who's she?
- My betrothed.

462
00:36:12.823 --> 00:36:16.327
Do you know what's happening
out there?

463
00:36:19.747 --> 00:36:20.748
No?

464
00:36:22.416 --> 00:36:23.918
Rhaenyra declared me dead.

465
00:36:24.919 --> 00:36:26.544
And after you disappeared.

466
00:36:26.545 --> 00:36:29.673
that little twat Daeron
decided he should be king.

467
00:36:32.968 --> 00:36:34.595
So. here's what
we're going to do.

468
00:36:36.597 --> 00:36:39.098
We're going to find Vhagar.

469
00:36:39.099 --> 00:36:42.101
fly to Tumbleton.
and put Daeron

470
00:36:42.102 --> 00:36:44.103
and that shitheel
Ormund in line.

471
00:36:44.104 --> 00:36:47.524
And then. we're all going
to march on King's Landing

472
00:36:47.525 --> 00:36:49.151
under my banner.

473
00:36:51.195 --> 00:36:55.032
And maybe. when Rhaenyra's
head is on a spike...

474
00:36:56.116 --> 00:36:57.659
and I'm back
on the Iron Throne...

475
00:36:57.660 --> 00:37:00.037
Aemond.

476
00:37:01.497 --> 00:37:03.457
Maybe then...

477
00:37:05.209 --> 00:37:06.544
I'll forgive you...

478
00:37:08.462 --> 00:37:11.048
for trying to fucking kill me.

479
00:37:15.678 --> 00:37:18.304
<i>Aside from the main gate.
there's one other way in.</i>

480
00:37:18.305 --> 00:37:21.099
A disused postern
on the northeast side.

481
00:37:21.100 --> 00:37:22.225
They've raised
wooden battlements

482
00:37:22.226 --> 00:37:24.185
but the defenses
are incomplete.

483
00:37:24.186 --> 00:37:26.145
so there are vulnerable areas.

484
00:37:26.146 --> 00:37:28.481
particularly the walls
to the southeast.

485
00:37:28.482 --> 00:37:29.817
Simple enough.

486
00:37:30.985 --> 00:37:32.987
I will burn the battlements
over the main gate.

487
00:37:33.988 --> 00:37:35.530
Once they're
clear of resistance.

488
00:37:35.531 --> 00:37:37.824
our van will lead the attack
with Caraxes for cover.

489
00:37:37.825 --> 00:37:40.326
Ulf and Silverwing
will guard the rear.

490
00:37:40.327 --> 00:37:41.995
Rhaenyra's banners will fly

491
00:37:41.996 --> 00:37:43.831
above the holdfast
by nightfall.

492
00:37:46.125 --> 00:37:49.211
Take every care to preserve the town
and its people. The realm is watching.

493
00:37:50.713 --> 00:37:53.172
The queen's moral standing
must remain absolute.

494
00:37:53.173 --> 00:37:54.340
Sounds boring.

495
00:37:54.341 --> 00:37:55.717
My prince.

496
00:37:55.718 --> 00:37:58.177
My lords.
Movement at the walls.

497
00:37:58.178 --> 00:38:01.682
The enemy has fortified
their numbers with children.

498
00:38:03.601 --> 00:38:05.518
Gods.

499
00:38:05.519 --> 00:38:07.186
- How many?
- Scores.

500
00:38:07.187 --> 00:38:08.605
All along the battlements.

501
00:38:08.606 --> 00:38:10.441
And that's just
what I could see.

502
00:38:12.526 --> 00:38:14.569
He's testing you. my prince.

503
00:38:14.570 --> 00:38:16.362
daring you
to use your dragon.

504
00:38:16.363 --> 00:38:17.907
The spineless cunt.

505
00:38:19.408 --> 00:38:22.202
Lord Roderick. are you still
prepared to die for our queen?

506
00:38:22.703 --> 00:38:24.037
Can't fucking wait.

507
00:38:24.038 --> 00:38:25.538
Take your greybeards
over the walls.

508
00:38:25.539 --> 00:38:27.874
overwhelm them with
your northern fighting spirit

509
00:38:27.875 --> 00:38:29.626
and open the gate
from within.

510
00:38:29.627 --> 00:38:32.795
But you are not to die
until you open the gate.

511
00:38:32.796 --> 00:38:34.632
Aye. gate open. then die.

512
00:38:36.258 --> 00:38:38.051
Lord Oscar will lead the flank
as planned.

513
00:38:38.052 --> 00:38:40.053
Ser Garibald has the reserve.

514
00:38:40.054 --> 00:38:41.972
The center is mine.

515
00:39:01.492 --> 00:39:03.910
This is the House of the Seven.

516
00:39:03.911 --> 00:39:06.455
No arms are to cross
its threshold.

517
00:39:07.456 --> 00:39:10.249
The people
of King's Landing gather.

518
00:39:10.250 --> 00:39:12.753
seeking to know
who is ordained to lead them.

519
00:39:14.296 --> 00:39:16.339
You will give them their answer

520
00:39:16.340 --> 00:39:18.341
by anointing me
for all to see.

521
00:39:18.342 --> 00:39:22.637
I have already told you
that such is impossible.

522
00:39:22.638 --> 00:39:25.807
And now. after Aegon and his dragon
have been resurrected.

523
00:39:25.808 --> 00:39:28.267
there could be no clearer sign

524
00:39:28.268 --> 00:39:32.106
of whom the gods
have chosen to rule. princess.

525
00:39:32.856 --> 00:39:34.191
I am queen.

